  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $14.69B (-1.6% 30D) keeps on-chain RWA exposure in a holding pattern\u2014tokenization momentum is still news- and pipeline-driven until distributed value breaks range. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/17/goldman-wells-fargo-morgan-stanley-see-tokenization-as-a-growth-play-not-a-threat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Goldman, Wells Fargo, Morgan Stanley see tokenization as a growth play, not a threat</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tradfi-and-fintech/tokenized-equities-reached-3-8-billion-this-year-dwf-labs-says\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tokenized Equities Reached $3.8 Billion This Year, DWF Labs Says</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Institutional commitments are still a leading share signal:</strong> Bank and asset-manager distribution deals often shift platform and network leadership before headline RWA totals fully catch up. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/nasdaq-tron-200m-atm-offering-fuel-trx-acquisitions?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nasdaq-listed Tron sets up $200M ATM share offering to fuel TRX acquisitions</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/can-the-sec-and-cftcs-pro-crypto-rules-be-overturned-legal-opinion?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Can the SEC and CFTC\u2019s pro-crypto rules be overturned? Legal opinion</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
